-- Doors, chests and switches on the dungeon maps (DungeonObjects.lua draws them). Our own short list:
-- what matters for finding the way and the loot, in our words. Positions are where each stands on
-- Blizzard's floor picture (0-1 across its 1002 x 668, as Data\DungeonBosses.lua), worked out by
-- tools\dungeon_marks.py from server spawn data used only as a reference; check them in game.
--   [instance mapID] = { [floor] = { { kind, x, y, name, note, count }, ... } }
--   floor = OpenMap's floor index (Data\OpenMapDungeonMaps.lua); out, out2... = the outside caves before it (Dungeon.lua OUTSIDE)
--   kind  = "locked" (a key or lockpicking), "event" (opens with a fight), "chest", "switch",
--           "quest" (a quest starts, ends or is about it), "npc" (a friendly quest giver, trainer or vendor),
--           "mob" (a monster a quest sends you to: a quest item it drops, or a kill), "patrol" (one that walks:
--           its way is in ns.DungeonPatrols)
--   note  = the tooltip's lines under the name ("" for none, a line break between lines); count = how many stand there
--   icon  = a switch's own icon (postbox, fire, rune, gear; else the lever); minor = true: drawn smaller and
--           fainter (things found all over a floor; Lua also counts "event" and "Sometimes here" as lesser)
